From b6e9f821ea2f29372b6a678d7a8aa4b233cf4523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:13:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Stop Acumatica login retries and per-request auth on
 status endpoints
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Containment for the 2026-07-31 Acumatica account lockout. The account recorded
exactly three failed password attempts about ten hours after the password was
rotated. Three is this client's signature.

Root cause in this repo: authenticate() went through the same _request_json
retry wrapper as every data read, with retries=2 feeding range(retries + 1). A
single request carrying a stale password therefore issued three
POST /entity/auth/login calls ~1.5s apart (0.5s, 1.0s backoff).

Made worse by two things: _build_dependencies() constructs a fresh client per
HTTP request, so nothing was ever reused; and platform_status() and
connector_status() both called fetch_branches(), which authenticates from
scratch. Those are the endpoints a monitor or dashboard polls on a timer, so
routine monitoring was issuing credential attempts.

Three changes:

1. Authentication is never retried. _request_json takes a per-call retries
   override; authenticate() passes 0. Data reads keep retrying — they carry a
   session, not a credential.

2. A rejected credential latches for the life of the process. Removing retries
   alone is not sufficient: with a client per request, an endpoint polled every
   30 seconds would still spend one attempt per poll and reach the threshold
   within minutes. After a rejection, later calls fail locally.

3. The connector is disabled by default. SCOREBOARD_ACUMATICA_ENABLED must be
   exactly "true" or nothing here contacts Acumatica. Fails closed, so a deploy
   that forgets it cannot resume authenticating.

Status endpoints now use status_snapshot(), which reports connector state
without authenticating and without disclosing credential material.

platform_status() no longer reads branches, so it reports
branch_mapping_state as "not_verified_no_acumatica_read" rather than deriving
"governed_complete" from an empty branch list. An empty list is not evidence
that every branch is mapped, and a status endpoint reporting unearned green is
worse than one reporting unknown.

Tests assert the exact number of network calls rather than just the outcome:
one login attempt not three, reads still retry, ten authenticate() calls
produce one attempt, a disabled connector makes zero calls, the flag fails
closed on TRUE/True/1/yes/on/empty, and status_snapshot() makes no call and
leaks no credential.

43 passed (37 pre-existing, 6 new).
